## 2. Functional Decomposition Diagram (FDD)

### What It Is
The FDD is a **hierarchical tree** diagram that breaks down the entire system into its major functions and sub-functions. It directly maps to your **Specific Objectives (A–L)** from Chapter 1.

### Structure

```
Level 0 (Top)     → The system name
Level 1 (Modules) → Your 12 specific objectives (A through L)
Level 2 (Sub)     → The sub-functions within each module
```

### Complete FDD Breakdown

#### Level 0: Chronicles of Arithmos

#### Level 1 → Level 2:

| Module | Sub-Functions |
|--------|--------------|
| **A. Battle Mechanics** | A.1 Time Progress Battle (TPB)<br>A.2 Turn Structure & Combat Menu<br>A.3 Resource Management (HP / MP / TP)<br>A.4 Tutorial Sequence<br>A.5 Training Hall System |
| **B. Math Battle System Plugin** | B.1 Equation Generator<br>B.2 Player Input Validation<br>B.3 Math Input Interface (GUI) |
| **C. Level-Based Difficulty System** | C.1 Basics (Lv 1–29): Addition / Subtraction<br>C.2 Intermediate (Lv 30–69): Multiplication / Division<br>C.3 Advanced (Lv 70–100): PEMDAS Equations<br>C.4 Training Dummy (Fixed / Dynamic Level) |
| **D. Content-Aware Timer System** | D.1 Complexity Analysis<br>D.2 Dynamic Timer Calculation<br>D.3 Operator-Based Time Bonus |
| **E. Enemy Auto-Scaling System** | E.1 Party Average Level Detection<br>E.2 Stat Scaling (HP / ATK)<br>E.3 Reward Scaling (EXP / Gold) |
| **F. Performance-Based Reward Mechanism** | F.1 Speed Detection<br>F.2 Correctness Validation<br>F.3 Multiplier Calculation (2.0x / 1.0x / 0.5x / 0x) |
| **G. Automatic Quest Generation** | G.1 Area Scanner<br>G.2 Enemy / Item Database Query<br>G.3 Quest Construction<br>G.4 Quest Log Tracker |
| **H. P2P Multiplayer** | H.1 Room Code Generation<br>H.2 PeerJS Connection Handler<br>H.3 Party Merging Logic<br>H.4 Data Synchronization |
| **I. Save System** | I.1 Manual Save (20 Slots)<br>I.2 Autosave (Map Checkpoints)<br>I.3 Load System |
| **J. Level-Based Progression** | J.1 EXP System<br>J.2 Gold / Currency System<br>J.3 Story Milestones |
| **K. Mobile Input System** | K.1 Device Detection<br>K.2 Virtual Numeric Keypad Display |
| **L. Game Assets & Entities** | L.1 Characters & NPCs<br>L.2 Enemies (5 Biomes)<br>L.3 Items & Equipment<br>L.4 Maps & Biomes<br>L.5 Audio (BGM / SFX)<br>L.6 Skills & Status Effects |

