## 4. How They Connect to Operational Feasibility

In your capstone guidelines, Section **4.3.1 Operational Feasibility** asks: *"Can this system realistically operate and solve the identified problem?"*

- The **Fishbone** proves that a real, multi-faceted problem exists (not just one vague issue) — showing the panelists exactly **what** your system addresses
- The **FDD** proves that you have a clear, organized functional plan for **how** the system will address each of those root causes through its 12 modules

```mermaid
graph LR
    A["Fishbone Diagram<br>(WHY the system is needed)"] --> B["FDD<br>(WHAT the system does)"]
    B --> C["Other Feasibility Sections<br>(HOW it's built)"]
    style A fill:#FF6B6B,color:#fff
    style B fill:#74B9FF,color:#fff
    style C fill:#55EFC4,color:#000
```

